Third-party material

FloraStack contains the following third-party code. None of it ships in the apps: it is test and
developer tooling. ATTRIBUTION.md records the source of each item and what it is used for.

- xtask/src/sha256.rs is adapted from PhotoCraft (https://github.com/storytold/photocraft), file
  xtask/src/sha256.rs, and the download flow of xtask/src/corpus/ follows its xtask/src/corpus.rs
  and xtask/src/pinned.rs, the archive flow included (as its PngSuite fetcher checks an archive).
  Copyright (c) 2026 ArtCraft Team and the PhotoCraft contributors.
  Licensed under the MIT License or the Apache License, Version 2.0, at your option; the license texts
  are the same as FloraStack's (LICENSE-MIT, LICENSE-APACHE).
- crates/testkit/src/lib.rs and xtask/src/ci.rs are adapted from LightCraft
  (https://github.com/storytold/lightcraft), files crates/testkit/src/lib.rs and xtask/src/ci_report.rs.
  Copyright (c) 2026 ArtCraft Team and the LightCraft contributors.
  Licensed under the MIT License or the Apache License, Version 2.0, at your option; the license texts
  are the same as FloraStack's (LICENSE-MIT, LICENSE-APACHE).

Third-party libraries in the apps

The apps are built with third-party crates under their own permissive licenses. Cargo.lock lists
every one, and the release packages will carry each license text (docs/ROADMAP.md, 7.1). These
need a mention here:

- LightCraft's crates lightcraft-tiff, lightcraft-codecs, lightcraft-meta, lightcraft-color,
  lightcraft-raw, lightcraft-pipeline, lightcraft-develop and lightcraft-raster, and through them
  lightcraft-geom and lightcraft-inpaint (https://github.com/storytold/lightcraft, commit
  a2a41383c4fd62fa85a46ccd00998639221f2d3c, release 0.10.0), which florastack-codecs and
  florastack-raw use.
  Copyright (c) 2026 ArtCraft Team and the LightCraft contributors.
  Licensed under the MIT License or the Apache License, Version 2.0, at your option; the license texts
  are the same as FloraStack's (LICENSE-MIT, LICENSE-APACHE).
  lightcraft-raw holds camera colour matrices derived from the camera spectral sensitivities,
  training reflectances and model alias list of rawtoaces-data
  (https://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/rawtoaces-data, v1.1.0), an Academy Software
  Foundation project licensed under the Apache License 2.0, and from the CIE 1931 colour-matching
  functions it ships (CIE, CC-BY-4.0). The matrices were fitted by the LightCraft contributors.
  lightcraft-inpaint ports the inpainting and Poisson membrane fill code of PhotoCraft
  (https://github.com/storytold/photocraft), Copyright the PhotoCraft contributors, licensed under
  the MIT License or the Apache License 2.0, at your option, as modified by the LightCraft
  contributors.
- jpeg-encoder (https://github.com/vstroebel/jpeg-encoder), the JPEG encoder inside
  lightcraft-codecs: this software is based in part on the work of the Independent JPEG Group.
